        "text": "Security update for the Linux Kernel (Live Patch 61 for SLE 12 SP5)",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for the Linux Kernel 4.12.14-122_231 fixes several issues.\n\nThe following security issues were fixed:\n\n- CVE-2022-50386: Bluetooth: L2CAP: Fix user-after-free (bsc#1250302).\n- CVE-2025-38499: clone_private_mnt(): make sure that caller has CAP_SYS_ADMIN in the right userns (bsc#1248673).\n- CVE-2025-21971: net_sched: Prevent creation of classes with TC_H_ROOT (bsc#1245794).\n- CVE-2025-38644: wifi: mac80211: reject TDLS operations when station is not associated (bsc#1248749).\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
